{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/BoundingBox"],"anchor":"k-d-trees","title":"k-d trees"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/Quadtree","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/Octree","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/SpatialItem"],"anchor":"Quadtrees-and-octrees","title":"Quadtrees and octrees"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/MXCIFOctree","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/MXCIFQuadtree","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/OverlappingPair","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/SpatialBoxItem"],"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/Trees"],"anchor":"Extended-Modules","title":"Extended Modules","generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree","type":"reference"},{"text":" holds a fixed set of points, SIMD vectors such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"SIMD2<Double>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"SIMD3<Float>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". It splits them at the median of the first coordinate, then each half at the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"median of the second, cycling through the dimensions, and keeps the result in one flat array"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with no links: every subtree is a contiguous run with its median in the middle."}]},{"code":["import SpatialTrees","","let tree = KDTree<SIMD2<Double>>([[2, 3], [5, 4], [9, 6], [4, 7], [8, 1], [7, 2]])","tree.nearestIndex(to: [9, 2])              \/\/ 4: the point [8, 1]","tree.nearestIndices(to: [9, 2], count: 2)  \/\/ [4, 5]","tree.indices(within: 3, of: [5, 5])        \/\/ [1, 3]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The six points split first on ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"x","type":"text"}]},{"text":" at the median [7, 2], then each side on ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"y","type":"text"}]},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertex","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Splits on"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Left subtree"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Right subtree","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"[7, 2]"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"x","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" = 7","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"[5, 4], [2, 3], [4, 7]","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"[9, 6], [8, 1]","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"[5, 4]"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"y","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" = 4","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"[2, 3]","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"[4, 7]"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"[9, 6]","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"y"}]},{"type":"text","text":" = 6"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"[8, 1]","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A search for the point nearest [9, 2] starts on the right of ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"x","type":"text"}]},{"text":" = 7, finds [8, 1] at distance","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"√2, and skips the whole left side, since the plane ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"x","type":"text"}]},{"text":" = 7 is 2 away, farther than that. Searches answer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the indices the points were given at, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/BoundingBox"},{"text":" describes a box for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree\/indices(in:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tree’s shape converts to Grafluent’s "},{"code":"BinaryTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryTree(_:)"},{"text":", whose vertices are","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the points’ indices."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/Quadtree","type":"reference"},{"text":" and an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/Octree","type":"reference"},{"text":" hold elements at points, and unlike a k-d tree take insertions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and removals as the points move. Each splits its region into four (eight) equal cells, and each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cell again, until every leaf holds at most a bucket of elements; a removal that leaves a cell’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"children holding no more than a bucket merges them back. Searches return ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/SpatialItem","type":"reference"},{"text":" values,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an element with its point.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["var map = Quadtree<String>(bounds: BoundingBox(lower: [0, 0], upper: [100, 100]))","map.insert(\"café\", at: [10, 20])","map.insert(\"station\", at: [80, 75])","map.nearest(to: [11, 19])?.element   \/\/ \"café\"","map.remove(\"café\", at: [10, 20])"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Their cells convert to Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"RootedTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"RootedTree(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so Grafluent draws the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subdivision.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spatialtrees"]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Trees over points in space that find the points nearest a query, or within a radius or a box."}],"metadata":{"title":"SpatialTrees","externalID":"SpatialTrees","roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"SpatialTrees"}],"role":"collection"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://SpatialTrees/documentation/SpatialTrees/KDTree/indices(in:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree\/indices(in:)","url":"\/documentation\/spatialtrees\/kdtree\/indices(in:)","type":"topic","title":"indices(in:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The indices of the points in ","type":"text"},{"code":"box","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", its faces included, ascending.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text